WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.724
After Tom had finished telling Joe and Huck about his trip to town, Joe and Huck were ready to go home.

2
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:13.051
Even Tom was tired of playing pirates and swimming, but he simply wasn't ready to return.

3
00:00:13.052 --> 00:00:17.820
Sure, he was homesick, and he thought of Aunt Polly and Becky all the time.

4
00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:22.313
But Tom now had a plan to make his return home a grand entrance.

5
00:00:22.314 --> 00:00:27.000
It meant waiting a while longer, and it meant the other boys would have to wait too.

6
00:00:27.001 --> 00:00:29.981
Tom didn't want to tell his friends about his plan yet.

7
00:00:29.982 --> 00:00:34.665
He was afraid that even his amazing plan would not be enough to keep them on the island.

8
00:00:34.666 --> 00:00:41.851
So he had to keep them interested in their adventure a little longer, even though it wouldn't be easy.

9
00:00:41.852 --> 00:00:45.550
Tom saw that Joe was sad, so he tried to cheer him up.

10
00:00:45.551 --> 00:00:49.316
"Let's look for buried treasure again," he said.

11
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:52.866
But Huck and Joe didn't want to look for treasure again.

12
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:58.430
Finally Joe said, "Let's give up. I want to go home."

13
00:00:58.431 --> 00:01:04.793
"Oh no," said Tom. "Just think of all the fishing here."

14
00:01:04.794 --> 00:01:07.287
"I don't care about fishing.

15
00:01:07.288 --> 00:01:11.879
I want to go home," said Joe, and he started to cry.

16
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:18.031
"What a baby," teased Tom. "You miss your mother, I bet."

17
00:01:18.032 --> 00:01:24.637
"I do," said Joe, "and you'd miss yours too, if you had one!"

18
00:01:24.638 --> 00:01:31.802
Tom became angry. "We'll let the crybaby go home, won't we, Huck?"

19
00:01:31.803 --> 00:01:35.240
"Y-yes," replied Huck sadly.

20
00:01:35.241 --> 00:01:37.367
Now Joe was angry.

21
00:01:37.368 --> 00:01:42.458
"Tom Sawyer, I'll never speak to you again for as long as I live!"

22
00:01:42.459 --> 00:01:48.749
"Who cares!" said Tom. "Go home. You're not a very good pirate.

23
00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:54.548
Huck and I aren't crybabies. We'll stay, won't we, Huck?"

24
00:01:54.549 --> 00:02:00.145
Tom didn't really want Joe to leave, but he was too angry to think of how he could make Joe stay.

25
00:02:00.146 --> 00:02:03.695
"I want to go too," said Huck quietly.

26
00:02:03.696 --> 00:02:06.487
"It's so lonely with just the three of us.

27
00:02:06.488 --> 00:02:11.710
If Joe goes, it'll be worse. Let's go too, Tom."

28
00:02:11.711 --> 00:02:14.738
Huck put on his hat and got ready to leave.

29
00:02:14.739 --> 00:02:17.865
He looked at Tom and said, "Think it over.

30
00:02:17.866 --> 00:02:20.073
We'll wait for you by the raft."

31
00:02:20.074 --> 00:02:22.644
Tom knew he was in trouble.

32
00:02:22.645 --> 00:02:28.132
His plan for a grand entrance was falling apart, and he couldn't think of a way to save it.

33
00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.971
"Wait forever if you want," said Tom angrily.

34
00:02:31.972 --> 00:02:35.697
"But I'm not going with you. I'm staying here."

35
00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:39.742
Joe and Huck began walking toward the raft.

36
00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:49.312
After a minute Tom ran after them, shouting, "Wait! Wait! I want to tell you something."

37
00:02:49.313 --> 00:02:52.185
Tom quickly told his friends about his idea.

38
00:02:52.186 --> 00:02:56.957
He promised that they could go home soon, just not today.

39
00:02:56.958 --> 00:02:59.027
Huck and Joe's spirits lifted.

40
00:02:59.028 --> 00:03:02.928
"Really, we'll go home on Sunday?" asked Joe.

41
00:03:02.929 --> 00:03:07.674
Tom smiled and said, "Yes, on Sunday."

42
00:03:07.675 --> 00:03:10.854
The boys dived into the river and played all day.

43
00:03:10.855 --> 00:03:16.602
That night they cooked and ate the rest of their food, and they retold the tales of their great adventure.

44
00:03:16.603 --> 00:03:22.855
Finally Tom explained that on Sunday they would float across the river on a log, so that no one would see them coming.

45
00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:28.515
Then they would sneak into church and hide under the large table by the entrance.

46
00:03:28.516 --> 00:03:34.068
On Sunday the whole town gathered in the church for Tom, Joe, and Huck's funeral.

47
00:03:34.069 --> 00:03:37.880
Everyone knew the boys, and they were all quite sad.

48
00:03:37.881 --> 00:03:43.796
Becky was the saddest of all. "Being mad was silly," she thought.

49
00:03:43.797 --> 00:03:47.492
"Now I'll never see Tom again."

50
00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:53.487
Aunt Polly and Joe's mother were sitting in the front of the church, and they were both dressed in black.

51
00:03:53.488 --> 00:03:57.849
After the opening prayer and hymn, the minister spoke about the boys.

52
00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:00.954
He told many stories about their good deeds.

53
00:04:00.955 --> 00:04:08.437
When the minister finished speaking, everyone was crying—even the minister himself.

54
00:04:08.438 --> 00:04:14.130
Earlier that morning the boys had hidden themselves under the table by the entrance of the church.

55
00:04:14.131 --> 00:04:18.796
They waited for the minister to finish his speech.

56
00:04:18.797 --> 00:04:21.856
Then they emerged from under the table.

57
00:04:21.857 --> 00:04:25.975
Tom proudly led his friends down the main aisle of the church.

58
00:04:25.976 --> 00:04:28.112
Everyone was shocked!

59
00:04:28.113 --> 00:04:33.402
Aunt Polly and Joe's mother shouted for joy, and they kissed the three boys wildly.

60
00:04:33.403 --> 00:04:36.777
Everyone else greeted the boys with relief and delight.

61
00:04:36.778 --> 00:04:47.375
The minister asked everyone to sing a hymn of thanksgiving, and the singing nearly took the church's roof off.

